WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.330
LEE JAE-YONG:
This is Lee Jae-Yong, known to the western

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.870
world as Jay Y. Lee.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:11.130
Jay is the grandson of the great Lee Byung-chul,
the founder of Samsung.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:15.799
Normally, these type of people are lazy spoiled
brats but not Jay.

00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:18.330
He’s actually done a lot grow Samsung.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:23.199
In fact, you could say that he’s the guy
who made Samsung into the multi hundred billion

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:25.100
juggernaut that they are today.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:29.300
But, this sort of wealth and power didn’t
come clean.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.360
It was the result of massive amounts of corruption.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:39.829
In fact, Jay was so corrupt that he got sentenced
to prison twice.

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:45.309
The first was a 5 year jail centence for bribery
and embezzlement and the second was a 2.5

00:00:45.309 --> 00:00:47.210
year sentence for bribery.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:52.180
Being the second richest man in Korea, I don’t
think you’d be surprised to hear that Jay

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:57.629
didn’t end up spending all that much time
in prison but that was completely fine.

00:00:57.629 --> 00:01:02.289
The prosecution’s main goal wasn’t to
put Jay behind bars to but to remove him from

00:01:02.289 --> 00:01:06.330
power, and publicly exposing him did exactly
that.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:12.500
For over 5 years, it seemed that the era of
Jay Y Lee’s Samsung was officially over.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:18.990
But out of nowhere, in August of 2022, South
Korean President Yoon Suk Yeol would pardon

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:19.990
Jay.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:25.110
And just two months later, Jay would return
to Samsung as chairman, a position that he’s

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.400
held ever since.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.510
Now, you might be jumping out of your seat
to blame President Yoon Suk Yeol.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:35.070
Of course, he’s just another bought out
politician that’s controlled by the super

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.070
rich.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:40.720
Now, that could very well be true but what
I can say is that the president didn't act

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:41.720
alone.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:47.219
You see, it was actually at America’s request
that President Yeol decided to pardon Jay.

00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:53.440
So, here’s the story of Jay’s insane rise
to power, his humiliating fall from grace,

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:58.659
and his unexpected return to the throne.

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:06.159
RISE TO POWER:
Taking a look back, the story of Jay dates

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:10.119
back to June 23, 1968 to Seoul, South Korea.

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:14.870
At the time, Samsung was already a thriving
business involved in a variety of industries

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:19.220
from grocery exports and textiles to insurance,
security, and retail.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:24.150
But, while Samsung was already successful,
they had yet to even enter the industries

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:28.250
that they’re most known for today: electronics
and appliances.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:32.430
And it would end up being Jay’s father,
Lee Kun Hee, who would lead this evolution

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.769
making him the chosen heir within the Samsung
family.

00:02:35.769 --> 00:02:40.319
Jay on the other hand was just a small boy
during all of this who was slowly working

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:41.670
his way through the school system.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.959
I don’t think you’d be surprised to hear
that Jay ended up attending the prestigious

00:02:45.959 --> 00:02:50.830
Seoul National University, the same university
that Sang Woo attended, where he majored in

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.460
East Asian history.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:56.530
He followed this up with an MBA from Keio
University before attending Harvard where

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:00.349
he spent 5 years trying to get a PhD in Business
Administration.

00:03:00.349 --> 00:03:04.989
Unfortunately though, he would never end up
finishing and just stuck to the family business

00:03:04.989 --> 00:03:07.340
which he joined in 1991.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:12.420
Speaking of joining the family business, let’s
just say that he had a royal welcome as he

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:17.549
would join directly as Vice President of Strategic
Planning at age 23.

00:03:17.549 --> 00:03:22.239
And shortly after this, he would be promoted
to Chief Customer Officer, a C suite position

00:03:22.239 --> 00:03:24.709
that was created specifically for Jay.

00:03:24.709 --> 00:03:30.110
Obviously, Jay largely benefited from nepotism
but that isn’t to say that Jay wasn’t

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.970
talented in his own right.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:36.560
After all, it’s not like all of Samsung’s
heirs have ended up as pivotal as Jay even

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.459
though they all got cushy executive positions.

00:03:39.459 --> 00:03:44.209
And the main reason for this is that Jay chose
to focus on the right sector of Samsung.

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:49.480
His sister, Lee Boo Jin for example, went
down the hospitality path and became the CEO

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.980
of Hotel Shilla, a luxury Korean hotel chain
associated with Samsung.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:58.370
Similarly, his other sister, Lee Seo Hyun,
went down the philanthropy route and became

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:01.270
the leader of Samsung’s welfare foundation.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:08.200
Our boy Jay, however, had bigger ambitions
and knew exactly where the future lay: electronics.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:12.370
This came in the form of 3 separate breakthroughs
starting with memory chips.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:17.940
In 1999, Samsung would develop the world’s
first 1 gb NAND flash and they would follow

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.780
this up with a ground breaking pace of innovation.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:35.670
2 gb in 2002, 4 gb in 2003, 8 gb in 2004,
16 gb in 2005, 32 gb in 2006, and 64 gb in

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:36.670
2007.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:40.729
Combine this rapid innovation with Samsung’s
resources, power, and connections, and I don’t

00:04:40.729 --> 00:04:45.650
think you’d be surprised to hear that Samsung
would end up as the king of memory.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:49.580
This would end up being really important as
this business is what would eventually bail

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.290
Jay out of jail.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:55.080
But this was just the beginning of Jay’s
contributions at Samsung.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.820
His next big contribution was TVs.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:01.919
Samsung didn’t necessarily create TVs that
were better than the competition but what

00:05:01.919 --> 00:05:05.030
they did do was market TVs better than the
competition.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:09.570
They attended all these tech events where
they showed off massive TVs, stupidly high

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.130
resolutions, and a bunch of marketing gimmicks.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:18.960
This included things like 3d tvs, curved tvs,
OLED, QLED, neo QLED and who knows what else.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.199
This isn’t to say that all of these technology
were just gimmicks.

00:05:22.199 --> 00:05:27.860
OLED for example is awesome technology but
what really sold this technology was Samsung’s

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:32.259
phenomenal marketing which has given them
the number 1 spot in the TV market for the

00:05:32.259 --> 00:05:36.860
past 17 years, and at the helm of all of it
was Jay.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:41.860
But if you thought memory and TVs were big,
you probably forgot that Samsung also dominates

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:45.080
another industry: smartphones.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:46.860
I don’t even think this one needs an explanation.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:50.360
Samsung has sold over 2 billion Galaxies itself.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:55.480
And according to Samsung, Jay has made invaluable
contributions to these sectors of Samsung.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:06:00.919
So, it’s no wonder why Jay was next in line
to take over the company but there would be

00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:05.440
a pretty big scare before this actually happened.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:15.190
LIKE FATHER LIKE SON:
In 2008, Jay’s father, Lee Kun-hee, would

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:17.440
resign from his position as chairman.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:20.030
Normally, this would be great news.

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:25.320
Lee had just completed a legendary run as
Samsung’s chairman and was retiring to make

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.500
way for younger generations right?

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:31.330
Well, that’s not exactly how this played
out.

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:34.599
Lee didn’t resign because he wanted to retire.

00:06:34.599 --> 00:06:37.490
He resigned because he was forced to retire.

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:43.669
You see, Lee was indicted on charges of tax
evasion, and he would end up with a 3 year

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:48.210
suspended sentence along with a $109 million
fine.

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:53.000
This itself was terrible publicity for Samsung
but what they were really worried about was

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.750
a potential political crisis.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:07:00.340
Prosecutors were also alleging that Samsung
had bribed influential South Korean politicians,

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:02.710
prosecutors, and bureacrats.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:07.780
And if this was proven in court, that would
truly be a disaster.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:12.370
Looking to avoid this, Lee and several of
his executives would resign which got the

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:15.840
prosecutors to back off and drop the bribery
charges.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:20.900
But while Lee was able to leave the situation
pretty clean, the same could not be said about

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:21.900
Jay.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:26.840
Lee had tarnished the family name making it
very difficult for Jay to ever takeover the

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:27.840
company.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.090
But, this duo wasn’t gonna go down so easily.

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:35.259
What they had to do was clear the family name
and they were willing to go to any length

00:07:35.259 --> 00:07:40.360
to do so including bribing the president of
South Korea: Lee Myung Bak.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:43.540
Also, this isn’t just speculation or something.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:48.150
Lee Myung Bak would eventually be sentenced
to 15 years in prison, partially for accepting

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.710
this bribe and pardoning Lee Kun-hee.

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:55.190
I think it’s safe to say that the former
president regretted accepting this bribe but

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:57.870
the same cannot be said about Lee Kun-hee.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:04.580
In 2010, Lee would return to Samsung as chairman
as a pardoned man making the bribe quite worth

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:05.580
it.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:09.940
And now that Lee was back in charge, his son
was also in the good graces of the company

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:12.000
who would make Jay vice chairman in 2012.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:17.430
As you can see, these mega companies and their
leaders have a billion different way to get

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.150
out of any situation.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.080
You get charged with tax evasion?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.080
No problem.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.610
You get charged with bribery?

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:24.620
No problem?

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:29.120
Obviously, you don’t wanna follow their
footsteps when it comes to any of these illicit

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.120
activities.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:35.149
But one aspect we can learn from is how these
companies are dealing with the high inflation

00:08:35.149 --> 00:08:40.060
high interest rate environment and their secret
is US treasury bills.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:44.769
All of the biggest companies in the world
own tens of billions if not hundreds of billions

00:08:44.769 --> 00:08:48.080
of dollars worth of US treasury bills including
Warren Buffett.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:52.990
And this is not surprising given that treasurys
are paying out historically high yields of

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:55.020
over 5%.

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:58.910
We wanted everyday people to be able to take
advantage of these high yields just like these

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:05.060
companies are doing, and that’s why we created
Silo, a modern bond investing platform.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:09.019
With Silo, you can invest in corporate and
government bonds all with the protection of

00:09:09.019 --> 00:09:14.589
$500,000 in SIPC insurance and $2.5 million
in FDIC insurance.

00:09:14.589 --> 00:09:18.950
So, if you would like to lock in high yields
for yourself from the comfort of your phone,

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:23.940
please consider checking out our bond investing
