00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:28.160
But anyway, while Lee was able to yeet out
of jail time, something he couldn’t yeet

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.890
out of was health concerns.

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:36.330
In 2014, Lee would suffer a heart attack and
though he did recover, this event would basically

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:42.030
make Jay the de facto chairman of Samsung
leading us into his own foray with the law.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:46.029
Given his family’s history, Jay was probably
involved in several shady activities over

00:09:46.029 --> 00:09:52.050
the years but the crime that got him arrested
was bribery of another South Korean president:

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.339
Park Geun-hye.

00:09:53.339 --> 00:09:57.959
It turns out that Jay had offered $38 million
worth of bribes to the presidents friends

00:09:57.959 --> 00:10:00.890
and acquaintances to push through a merger.

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:05.600
Samsung had no choice but to admit that they
had indeed handed over this money but they

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:10.720
would insist that it was merely a good faith
donation and that Jay had no idea that these

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:13.120
people were connected to the president.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:19.630
That was obviously complete and utter BS and
unsurprisingly, Jay would be found guilty

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:25.089
of perjury, embezzlement, and bribery leading
to a 5 year prison sentence.

00:10:25.089 --> 00:10:29.290
Something else that isn’t surprising is
that Jay never ended up spending 5 years in

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.290
prison.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:33.810
After spending 1 year in prison, the Seoul
High Court would magically reduce his sentence

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:38.250
to 2.5 years and suspend it, meaning that
he was let go.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:42.240
Unfortunately for Jay though, the Supreme
Court of South Korea would end up ordering

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:47.300
a retrial which resulted in another 2.5 year
prison sentence for Jay in early 2021.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:52.230
By this point, Jay had already pulled all
the strings he could to minimize his stay

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:57.090
in prison and all he could do was just put
his head down and serve his sentence.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:01.480
That was until America decided to get involved.

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:10.800
RETURN TO THE THRONE:
If you’ve been following the tech world,

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:14.820
you’re probably familiar with the chip shortage
that we went through recently.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:19.019
Whether you were buying a Tesla or a regular
old refrigerator, you often had to wait several

00:11:19.019 --> 00:11:23.060
months or even more than an year just to get
your product.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:27.529
And the main reason for this was the supply
chain shortage, and more specifically, the

00:11:27.529 --> 00:11:28.700
chip shortage.

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:33.220
On one side, this was great for businesses
as they could jack up prices and capitalize

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:34.930
on limited supply.

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:39.630
But on the other hand, they were missing out
on a lot of demand simply because they couldn’t

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.340
meet the demand.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:45.680
Not to mention, all of this was making President
Joe Biden look pretty bad.

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:50.200
So, America turned to Samsung and TSMC to
fix this issue.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:55.279
Unfortunately for them though, Lee Kun-hee
would pass away in late 2020 meaning that

00:11:55.279 --> 00:11:59.130
Samsung needed a new leader to navigate this
supply chain crisis.

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:04.600
And who better for the job than the prodigy
son with shady ethics: Jay Y Lee.

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:06.680
How could they get Jay out of prison though?

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:12.930
Easy, by leveraging the largest lobbying group
in America: the United States Chamber of Commerce.

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:18.510
If you’re wondering who funds this lobbying
group, well, they don’t disclose their donors,

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:22.019
but some companies are transparent about their
affiliation.

00:12:22.019 --> 00:12:27.380
This includes the likes of FedEx, Facebook,
Microsoft, Cheron, Comcast, Ford, and Pfizer.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:30.579
So, yeah, a pretty powerful group.

00:12:30.579 --> 00:12:35.720
And in 2021, these guys would approach South
Korean president Yoon Suk Yeol with “a proposal”

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:37.930
to solve the global chip shortage.

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:43.220
This plan started off by getting Jay out of
prison in August of 2021 on parole, just 7

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:45.550
months after he was sentenced for the second
time.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:50.339
This parole, however, came along with a 5
year restriction on business activities, so

00:12:50.339 --> 00:12:54.529
Jay couldn’t just immediately return to
Samsung but that was ok.

00:12:54.529 --> 00:12:58.490
It was better for Jay to lay low for a while
and wait for people to forget before returning

00:12:58.490 --> 00:12:59.800
anyway.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.930
And that’s exactly what would happen.

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:06.860
12 months after getting released, President
Yoon Suk Yeol would pardon Jay in August of

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.010
2022.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:12.649
His reasoning was that Jay was simply too
important to the Korean economy to be kept

00:13:12.649 --> 00:13:13.779
in jail.

00:13:13.779 --> 00:13:18.300
Outraged by this pardon, activists would protest
on the streets but this didn’t stop Jay

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:21.519
from returning as chairman in October of 2022.

00:13:21.519 --> 00:13:26.850
Since then, memory chip prices have fallen
off a cliff as much 53% actually.

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:31.339
In fact, memory chip prices have fallen so
much that Samsung’s own profits have fallen

00:13:31.339 --> 00:13:34.900
by 95% within just 1 year.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:40.410
Is this because of some strings that Jay pulled
or just a result of the market naturally correctly?

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:45.290
We may never know but this doesn’t really
matter for Jay or the lobbyists because things

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:47.899
played out just fine for them.

00:13:47.899 --> 00:13:52.630
And that’s how a convict ended up as the
new chairman of Samsung.

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:56.640
Jay may be back but he’s definitely feeling
the pain of falling memory chip prices and

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.630
more importantly the era of peak smartphone.

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:05.000
Check out this video to learn more.

